                <pb facs="0919" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A14/462½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-03T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 3,
                                1928—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>341. Your despatch No. 7615 of June 21, 1927. Please ascertain discreetly and
                    telegraph results of proposed conference of three Powers with Abyssinia and
                    present status of arms traffic control.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
